Credits
=======

The Hyprland configuration and several tool configs in this repository began
as the Caelestia dotfiles by soramane and contributors, GPL-3.0:
https://github.com/caelestia-dots/caelestia

config/miscellaneous/eduroam-fontys.py is the eduroam CAT Linux installer
generated for Fontys Hogescholen, by the GEANT project (Tomasz Wolniewicz,
Michal Gasewicz and contributors), with a small ChiropteraOS patch to how it
saves the CA certificate: https://cat.eduroam.org

share/chiroptera/plugins/ holds three Chiroptera Shell plugins that config.toml
enables, vendored so a new account needs no online catalog. All are MIT, with
their notices in each plugin's LICENSE:
- arch-updater (yuuto/arch-updater) by yuuto, version 2.0.3. Its manifest
  declares the MIT license; the upstream folder had no LICENSE file, so the
  standard MIT text naming its author was added.
- obs-control (ayagmar/obs-control) by ayagmar, version 1.0.0.
- w-engine (tadomika_ari/w-engine) by TadomiKa-Ari, version 1.4.0, from the
  community catalog at commit cea27fb70c53. Its manifest declares the MIT
  license; the upstream folder had no LICENSE file, so the standard MIT text
  naming its author was added.
ChiropteraOS changes: they call the plugin API and the CLI by the shell's own
name, their docs name Chiroptera Shell, and the catalog thumbnails are left out.
w-engine also finds the Workshop in every Steam library libraryfolders.vdf
lists and hands linux-wallpaperengine the wallpaper's folder and that library's
Wallpaper Engine assets (the engine searches the default library only), puts
wallpapers on the background layer when none is chosen (the engine's default,
bottom, covers the shell's desktop widgets), and its panel shows 24 wallpapers
a page instead of 48 and reads each project.json once (a 48-tile page overran
the shell's per-call CPU budget, which turns the panel off).

config/chiroptera/templates/zen-browser/ derives from the zen-browser template
formerly bundled with Chiroptera Shell, MIT (notice in its LICENSE), with the
palette split by color scheme for live recoloring. Its apply.sh is ChiropteraOS's
own.
